{#
  The success page after converting. Reached from the check page via the
  POST-then-GET redirect in controller.js, so refreshing doesn't resubmit.

  Consolidation fix (id-threading): "View the guidance" used to always
  open the editor with no id at all, showing its fixed "SFI 23" sample
  regardless of what was actually just converted — one of the three
  id-threading bugs the plan's crawl found. There's no real
  guidanceDocuments entry to pass an id for (this flow's details are
  session-only — it does not create a real tracked Draft document, an
  explicitly confirmed scope choice, not an oversight).

  Revised fix: "View the guidance" now opens the document overview page
  (consolidated/document/:id) rather than the editor directly, matching
  every other "View"/document link in the consolidated build. That page
  has no missing-id fallback (unlike the editor's own ?title= workaround,
  still used elsewhere) — it 404-redirects to the hub instead — so
  controller.js hardcodes guideId to one real, existing, genuinely
  Published document (sfi-nutrient-management-actions, CONVERTED_GUIDE_ID
  there — see that constant's own comment for why, not the more obviously
  "on-theme" sfi-soil-health-actions) rather than inventing
  draft-persistence for a genuinely new tracked entry. The panel above
  still shows the guide name actually entered; the overview page it links
  to shows that hardcoded document's own title/description instead — a
  known mismatch accepted as part of this scope choice.

  Consolidation decision: no "edit this guide" CTA is added here — the
  plan's brief confirmed the confirmation page's only real links are "View
  the guidance" and "Convert another document"; View already opens the
  overview page (with Edit from there), so a separate Edit link would just
  duplicate it.
#}
{% extends "common/layouts/content.njk" %}

{% from "govuk/components/panel/macro.njk" import govukPanel %}
{% from "govuk/components/button/macro.njk" import govukButton %}

{% set pageName = "Guidance converted" %}

{% block columns %}

  {{ govukPanel({
    titleText: "Guidance converted",
    text: guideName
  }) }}

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">What happens next</h2>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    Your document is now markdown in the hub, saved as a draft. Only you can
    see it until it is reviewed and published.
  </p>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    Have a look at how it converted before you take it any further.
  </p>

  {{ govukButton({
    text: "View the guidance",
    href: "/consolidated/document/" + guideId
  }) }}

  <p class="govuk-body">
    <a class="govuk-link" href="/consolidated/upload">Convert another document</a>
  </p>

{% endblock %}
